US-004 is only partly done. The local gates now pass on every platform I can run here, but the hosted CI jobs have never run on GitHub, so Windows/MSVC and Linux/Clang are not verified by CI yet.

**What was blocking the gates**
- `tests/src/core_assert_tests.cpp:38` passed `ENGINE_ASSERT` (a statement macro) to `CHECK_NOTHROW`. This broke both Linux clang and MSVC. I wrapped it in a function, as the later tests in that file already were.
- `engine/core/src/file_io.cpp`: `create_directories` now classifies an existing non-directory as `AlreadyExists` before calling `std::filesystem`. The libstdc++ error code differed from what the test expects, so the result depended on the platform.
- `engine/core/include/engine/core/guid.hpp`: renamed the `hash` local that shadowed `std::hash` under GCC `-Wshadow` with `-Werror`.

**Local gate results (current tree)**
- Offline Linux clang (`tools/ci/offline_verify.sh`, `unshare -rn`, only `lo`, `build/linux-dev` removed first): passed, 10/10.
- Linux GCC 9.4 (`linux-gcc`, `linux-gcc-debug`, `linux-gcc-unit`): passed, 10/10.
- Linux ASan/UBSan (`linux-asan`, `linux-sanitize`): passed, 10/10.
- Windows MSVC 14.51 (`ValidateVendor`, `win-dev`, `win-debug`, `win-unit`): passed, 10/10.

**Still open**
- The hosted GitHub Actions jobs have not run. CI pins clang-14 and GCC 11, but only clang 10 and GCC 9.4 were tested locally. `docs/build.md` records this gap.
- GPU jobs: no GPU runner is available here, so the status stays `not-run` (hosted CI) or `unsupported` (runner present, no GPU suite yet). Neither counts as passed.
- `engine_bench --suite acceptance` does not apply yet; the benchmark harness is US-074.

